==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*skīnaną}}, from an {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} root {{m|ine-pro|*skai-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ski-}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|skīna}} ({{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|skine}}, {{m|fy|skyne}}), {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|skīnan}} ({{etyl|nds|-}} {{m|nds|schienen}}), {{etyl|odt|-}} {{m|odt|skīnan}} ({{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|schijnen}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|skīnan}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|scheinen}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|skína}} ({{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|skinne}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|skina}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍃𐌺𐌴𐌹𐌽𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|σκιά}}, {{etyl|sla-pro|-}} {{m|sla-pro|*sěnь}} ({{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|сень}}).

